# Rules + skills for agents

When acting as the parent/orchestrator in this repo:

1. Treat `AGENTS.md` as the index for `.cursor/rules/` and `.cursor/skills/`.
2. Before non-trivial work, pick skills via `.cursor/skills/using-agent-skills/SKILL.md` and follow those skills.
3. Apply `.cursor/rules/project-memory.mdc` on every task. Do not pull analytics, pipeline, CI, or backend-framework rules from other products; they are not in this repo.
4. When launching subagents (`codebase-explorer`, `full-stack-engineer`, `qa-engineer`), include in the Task prompt:
   - goal and constraints;
   - paths of applicable rules, including `.cursor/rules/project-memory.mdc`, for layout or a new feature `.cursor/rules/ui-quality.mdc`, and for any behavior change `.cursor/rules/test-pyramid.mdc`;
   - paths of applicable skills, including `.cursor/skills/ui-quality/SKILL.md` when the task changes layout or adds a feature, and `.cursor/skills/test-pyramid/SKILL.md` when behavior changes or tests are added.
5. Subagents start with a clean context — they will not see this chat unless you hand off that detail.
